<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich von Plauen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1370–<a href="/years/1429">1429</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Heinrich von Plauen the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich von <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plauen">Plauen</a> was a knight of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> from the family of the reeves of Plauen in the Vogtland. After the order's defeat at Grunwald in 1410 he organised the successful defence of Marienburg against Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, and he was elected Grand Master. Deposed in 1413 after quarrels within the order, he spent years in confinement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-plauen.jpg" alt="Heinrich von Plauen" width="204" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous plate · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_V_von_Plauen.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
